      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Write to a File Using ofstream"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In order to use the ofstream class, we first need to import the <fstream> header file. Then, we can create an ofstream object to open a file in write mode."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "// create ofstream object\nofstream my_file;\n\n// open cpp.txt file in write mode\nmy_file.open(\"cpp.txt\");"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Notice that we don't need to supply ios::out as an argument to the open() function. This is because the open() function of ofstream has ios::out as a default argument."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Idea Emoji",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Now, let's write a program to write to cpp.txt using ofstream."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "#include <iostream>\n\n#include <fstream>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n\n    string content;\n\n\n    // create ofstream object\n    ofstream my_file;\n\n    // open file for writing\n    my_file.open(\"cpp.txt\");\n\n\n    // check if the file has opened properly\n    if (my_file.fail()) {\n\n        // print error message\n        cout << \"File failed to load!\";\n\n        // exit the program\n        exit(0);\n    }\n\n\n    // write to the file\n    my_file << \"C++ supports writing to files.\" << endl;\n    my_file << \"We can use both fstream and ofstream to write.\";\n\n\n    // close the file\n    my_file.close();\n\n    return 0;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Now, the contents of cpp.txt will be"
